      "description_en": "Located in Cefalà Diana near Palermo, this Arab-era thermal ruin with its 10th-century arched architecture and naturally heated pool forms one of the least known but most impressive footprints of Sicily's Islamic heritage. Frequently visited by Palermitans, this rest area is a place tourists have not yet fully discovered.",
